{"about_the_game":"<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3863410/extras/7c39b0c17f522f2105ecc75d27c24500.webp?t=1753986201\" width=616 height=56 /></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Novella Divina</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Created by a single developer, inspired by Dante's Divine Comedy, Friedrich Nietzsche\u2019s Thus Spoke Zarathustra, and the profound mysteries of Alexander Scriabin. A tender attempt to express a <strong>personal philosophy</strong> through the delicate charm of catgirls \u2014 a philosophy whose central idea is: <i><strong>\u201cArt as Meaning.\u201d</strong></i></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3863410/extras/4c421aec8552126898195c56f6a32408.webp?t=1753986201\" width=616 height=51 /></span> </p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Characters</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Three enchanting catgirls</strong>, each with her own personality and personal struggles...</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Strange, Slavic-fairytale-mythical beings...</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You are the <strong>Hero</strong>.</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3863410/extras/cd51605deab32aa138f82a65b2e5e0b4.webp?t=1753986201\" width=616 height=51 /></span> </p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Story</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Transported to an unfamiliar world, you begin to hear the <strong>melodies of life itself</strong>...<br>Upon meeting three gentle, long-eared sisters, your mission becomes clear: at any cost, stop the <i><strong>Musical Ether</strong></i>, for it brings ever-growing suffering and hopeless despair to the catgirls and other beings...</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span c